╭─ Issue description ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Issue Title: [BUG] SSE transport connection passes an invalid argument to MCP's client class                                                    │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Description:                                                                                                                                    │
│ ### Description                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ When initializing an MCP client while creating a connection to an MCP server using SSE transport, an invalid argument (`terminate_on_close`) is │
│ passed. The argument is valid for                                                                                                               │
│ (https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/blob/main/src/mcp/client/streamable_http.py#L452C5-L452C23), but is not supported for [SSE  │
│ transport](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/blob/main/src/mcp/client/sse.py#L25-L32). This results in a crash when trying to  │
│ run an agent that connects to an MCP server using SSE transport.                                                                                │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Steps to Reproduce                                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ 1. Start an MCP server using the (https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23605043/server.py) script                                          │
│ 2. Run the (https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23605064/agent.py) script where an agent tries to use the MCP server                      │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Expected behavior                                                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ The agent successfully establishes a connection to the MCP server                                                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Screenshots/Code snippets                                                                                                                   │
